      'imp-917-partial-kk (commit 180fd5d): added scripts/imp-917-run-cell.mjs --verify-prototype-env-readers, a broader input-side content-level check that extends partial-gg (--verify-prototype-schema) from a single-token assertion (process.env.IMP857_EPSILONS only) to an all-six-tokens assertion across every IMP857_* env-var reader the driver binds to per cell: IMP857_N, IMP857_DT, IMP857_NSTEPS, IMP857_K0, IMP857_PHASEVEL, IMP857_EPSILONS. Closes the silent-drift gap partial-gg only partially closed — where a non-EPSILONS reader (e.g. IMP857_K0) is renamed, deleted, or restructured between imp-917 infrastructure work and the ~20 CPU-hour offline run, the prototype would still spawn, still read EPSILONS, and silently fall back to its in-source default (k0 = Math.PI for IMP857_K0; 0.0003 / 0.0001 for IMP857_DT; etc.) and measure the wrong resonance with no up-front diagnostic. The new check reads the prototype via readFileSync once and filters PROTOTYPE_ENV_READER_TOKENS against content.includes(t), so the failure message names every missing token rather than stopping at the first. Introduces a new PROTOTYPE_ENV_READER_TOKENS module-level constant (array of 6) and a new checkPrototypeEnvReaders() helper returning {ok, path, tokens, missing, error} — shaped as a deliberate superset of checkPrototypeSchema() return ({ok, path, token, error}) with tokens (array) + missing (array) instead of the single token, so a future --verify-prototype-env-readers-json analog and aggregate-step wiring can reuse it without drift, matching the partial-gg -> partial-hh -> partial-ii -> partial-jj shell-first / JSON-second / shell-aggregate / JSON-aggregate cadence used for every other discrete check. On success prints the OK line naming the path and all 6 tokens and exits 0; on failure prints a specific FAILED diagnostic naming the missing reader(s) and exits 1. Orthogonal to --verify-prototype-schema: the narrow single-EPSILONS check remains (cheap, unambiguous, failure mode most likely to surface since EPSILONS is the only array / most-often-edited parameter); the broader 6-reader check adds defense-in-depth without changing or duplicating the narrow check. Shell-only for this partial; --verify-prototype-env-readers-json analog and --preflight / --preflight-json wiring can follow in future partials. Implementation is strictly additive: one JSDoc paragraph in the header block (placed immediately after --verify-prototype-schema-json so reading order matches handler order), one --help usage-string line, one parseArgs flag slot (verifyPrototypeEnvReaders), one parseArgs case branch, one module-level PROTOTYPE_ENV_READER_TOKENS constant, one checkPrototypeEnvReaders() helper, and a ~15-line handler placed immediately after the --verify-prototype-schema-json handler. No refactor of existing helpers (checkPrototypeSchema() unchanged, PROTOTYPE_SCHEMA_TOKEN unchanged), no parseArgs refactor, no behavioural change on any existing flag. Verified locally: --verify-prototype-env-readers emits the OK line naming the path and all 6 tokens and exit=0; --verify-prototype-schema still emits the OK line byte-for-byte identical to partial-gg (refactor-invariant, helper unchanged); --verify-prototype-schema-json still emits {ok:true, path:<resolved>, token:"process.env.IMP857_EPSILONS", error:null} and exit=0; --preflight still emits 7 step banners + "imp-917 --preflight PASS: all 7 steps OK" with exit=0 (aggregated pre-flight unchanged; new check not yet wired in). npm run build completes in 4.49s with no new warnings. Also finalised partial-jj commit hash ("this commit" -> e6800c7).',
