      'imp-917-partial-bbbbbbbbb (commit 1b91f9b): added scripts/imp-917-run-cell.mjs --remaining-cells, a progress-aware shell emitter that diffs IMP_896_RETUNING_CALIBRATION.missingCells against IMP_857_PHASED_FORCING_SWEEP.measuredRows and prints only the (N, eps) cells still needing offline-worker time. Pivots away from the saturated --batch-plan-cost-triple-*mean power-mean axis (now seventy exponents x {shell, JSON} = one hundred forty siblings spanning p in {-1, 0, 1..68}) to a genuinely orthogonal progress-tracking concern. Imports IMP_857_PHASED_FORCING_SWEEP from src/data/imp-857-phased-forcing-sweep.js, builds a Set of `${N}|${eps}` keys from measuredRows, filters MISSING_CELLS to entries whose key is NOT in that set, and prints a column-aligned ASCII table (idx, N, eps, dt, nSteps, wallSecEst) plus a footer with the remaining-row count and triple-amortized wallSecondsEstimate (sum c.wallSecondsEstPerTripleRun / 3, matching the IMP_896_RETUNING_CALIBRATION.totalWallSecondsEstimate convention exactly). Distinct from --missing-cells (the static infrastructure-time list, always 14 rows): this list shrinks by one each time the offline worker completes a cell and appends its measured row, so an operator running mid-batch can tell at a glance which cells still need CPU time without manually cross-referencing imp-896-retuning-calibration.js and imp-857-phased-forcing-sweep.js. Pure data emitter (exit 0 unconditionally) matching the --missing-cells / --retuning-table cadence; not a check, not wired into --preflight / --preflight-json. Atomic: one import line for IMP_857_PHASED_FORCING_SWEEP, one parseArgs out-object slot (remainingCells: false), one parseArgs case-branch (out.remainingCells = true), one Usage-block header line, one --help usage-string line, one new handler block immediately after args.missingCellsJson; no new helper, no refactor, no change to existing flags. Smoke verified locally: --remaining-cells emits the full 14-row table (currently all 14 still pending since MEASURED_ROWS only covers eps in {0, 0.01, 0.05} for N in {1000, 2000} which has no overlap with MISSING_CELLS) with footer "remaining: 14 rows, wallSecondsEstimate ~= 152800 s (~42.4 CPU-hours, triple-amortized)" matching IMP_896_RETUNING_CALIBRATION.totalWallSecondsEstimate exactly (152800 s = 42.444 h); --missing-cells still emits its 14-row body byte-identical; --verify-plan still emits OK with 14 MISSING_CELLS covered exactly; npm run build passes cleanly in 4.54s with no new warnings. Ticket kept pending; completedByModel/completedByChannel NOT added because the ~20 CPU-hour offline execution of the 14 measurement rows remains the honest closure condition. --remaining-cells is the operator-facing progress probe that will keep working as MEASURED_ROWS grows during the offline batch. Also finalised partial-aaaaaaaaa commit hash ("this commit" -> 89ba14f).',
